            <ArticleTitle>Streptococcal myositis and the acute abdomen: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>328-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous streptococcal myositis, previously rare, is now reported more frequently. The condition is caused by overwhelming group A beta-haemolytic streptococcal infection and is not necessarily fatal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
